    "created_at": "2017-06-15T23:48:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-06-15T23:48:26Z",
    "body": "The second half of the [\"Timing model concepts\"](https://w3c.github.io/web-animations/#timing-model-concepts) section describes the integration of Web Animations with this processing model but its somewhat placeholder text at this stage. Perhaps we could reword \"run CSS animations and send events\" to \"update declarative animations and send animation events\". Then we can refer back to that definition from Web Animations / CSS animations / CSS transitions.\r\n\r\nLong-term when CSS animations and transitions are speced in terms of Web Animations we can drop the \"passing in now as the timestamp\" part.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
